 "overview": "The MPS School Committee oversees the district's budget, facilities, and academic policies during a period marked by leadership transitions and significant infrastructure planning. Following the departure of the previous superintendent, the body appointed and eventually formalized a permanent leader to guide the district through multi-year strategic goals [M19, M21, M49, M65]. Major work includes navigating a multi-million dollar high school building project with the state and addressing critical overcrowding at the elementary level [M24, M30, M61]. The committee also manages ongoing labor negotiations and adapts graduation requirements to align with evolving state standards [M31, M26]. As of October 2026, the body is finalizing a new district strategic plan and formalizing elementary school reassignment policies [M65, M67].",
