  {
   "name": "Elementary school overcrowding and reconfiguration",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Addressing capacity issues at the Roberts Elementary School has been a primary concern, leading to the relocation of preschool classrooms to create space [M06, M35]. The committee reviewed various space utilization studies and conducted community surveys to explore district-wide restructuring, including moving to K-4, 5-6, and 7-8 grade spans [M44, M45]. To ensure adequate planning and financial stability, the committee voted to delay the earliest implementation of any 5-8 grade reconfiguration until the 2028-2029 school year [M63]. Recent work focuses on formalizing a policy to manage intra-district reassignment requests and enrollment buffers [M67].",
