   "name": "Capital infrastructure and HVAC upgrades",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee has authorized several large-scale capital projects to address aging facility systems, beginning with a $25.7 million bond for HVAC replacements at the McGlynn and Andrews schools [M20, M29]. These projects shifted toward construction in late 2025, while the committee simultaneously identified over $83 million in broader district-wide repair needs through a facilities assessment [M43, M46]. In 2026, the body approved a $22.7 million schematic design for HVAC electrification and roof replacement at Roberts Elementary [M61, M64]. The district continues to update multi-year capital plans to prioritize maintenance and safety improvements [M51, M64].",
