   "summary": "Early in the term, the committee addressed significant waitlists for after-school care by partnering with City Year and authorizing additional site coordinator positions [M01, M08, M38]. Following a consultancy with the Belmont Afterschool Enrichment Collaborative (BASIC), the district approved a major restructuring of its programs in 2026 to add 150 seats [M55]. This expansion involved the creation of new full-time site director roles and a tiered tuition rate card [M55, M63]. By late 2026, the district reported a 68% reduction in the after-school waitlist [M65].",
